Subject: server: use the C RTL's getopt() on VMS

OpenVMS has getopt() in the C RTL (declared in <unistd.h>) but no
<getopt.h>, so server.c compiled its own fallback getopt()/optarg/optind.
The compiler maps those CRTL names to DECC$GETOPT etc., and the link then
reports them as defined twice (%ILINK-W-MULDEF against DECC$SHR).  Use the
CRTL's on VMS.

--- a/src/server.c
+++ b/src/server.c
@@ -50,6 +50,8 @@
 
 #ifdef HAVE_GETOPT_H
 # include <getopt.h>
+#elif defined(__VMS)
+# include <unistd.h>     /* getopt() is in the C RTL; there is no getopt.h */
 #else
 /* basic (very limited) getopt() implementation */
 extern char *optarg;
